Subject: fix(triage): accept an issue URL on the configured GitHub host

tracker_validate_issue_url matches https://github.com by name, so a valid
issue URL on any enterprise install is rejected before the triage agent does
anything:

  ERROR: ISSUE_URL does not match expected pattern: https://forge.internal/acme/widgets/issues/79

tracker_parse_issue_url strips the same literal host, so even where validation
passed the repository would be parsed wrongly.

Take the host from GITHUB_SERVER_URL, defaulting to https://github.com, which
is what scripts/pre-code-jira.sh already does for its run URLs. Behaviour on
github.com is unchanged.

The host is compared as a literal prefix rather than interpolated into the
regex, so a server URL containing regex metacharacters cannot change what the
pattern means, and the path is still matched exactly as strictly as before.
Parsing uses parameter expansion for the same reason.

The change is made in scripts/lib/github-triage-ops.lib.sh and mirrored into
the two generated scripts that embed it, scripts/pre-triage.sh and
scripts/post-triage.sh, which a build would otherwise regenerate.

Breadboard note: this patches fullsend-ai/agents, not fullsend-ai/fullsend, and
is applied to the agents mirror by deploy/fullsend/seed/seed-upstream-agents.py.
Written to be sent upstream as-is. Add a DCO sign-off before submitting it as a
human-authored change.

diff --git a/scripts/lib/github-triage-ops.lib.sh b/scripts/lib/github-triage-ops.lib.sh
index db7908e..9aef3e3 100755
--- a/scripts/lib/github-triage-ops.lib.sh
+++ b/scripts/lib/github-triage-ops.lib.sh
@@ -19,14 +19,26 @@ GITHUB_TRIAGE_OPS_SH_LOADED=1
 # --- URL handling ---
 
 tracker_validate_issue_url() {
-  if [[ ! "${ISSUE_URL}" =~ ^https://github\.com/[a-zA-Z0-9._-]+/[a-zA-Z0-9._-]+/issues/[0-9]+$ ]]; then
+  # The issue lives on whichever GitHub the run is executing against, which
+  # GITHUB_SERVER_URL names. Matching github.com by name rejects a valid URL on
+  # any enterprise install. The host is compared as a literal prefix rather
+  # than interpolated into the regex, so a server URL containing regex
+  # metacharacters cannot change what the pattern means.
+  local server="${GITHUB_SERVER_URL:-https://github.com}"
+  server="${server%/}"
+  local rest="${ISSUE_URL#"${server}/"}"
+  if [[ "${rest}" == "${ISSUE_URL}" ]] || \
+     [[ ! "${rest}" =~ ^[a-zA-Z0-9._-]+/[a-zA-Z0-9._-]+/issues/[0-9]+$ ]]; then
     echo "ERROR: ISSUE_URL does not match expected pattern: ${ISSUE_URL}" >&2
     return 1
   fi
 }
 
 tracker_parse_issue_url() {
-  REPO=$(echo "${ISSUE_URL}" | sed 's|https://github.com/||; s|/issues/.*||')
+  local server="${GITHUB_SERVER_URL:-https://github.com}"
+  server="${server%/}"
+  REPO="${ISSUE_URL#"${server}/"}"
+  REPO="${REPO%%/issues/*}"
   ISSUE_NUMBER=$(basename "${ISSUE_URL}")
 }
 
